        "verdict": "needs-attention",
        "topFinding": "The verdict moves to needs-attention because the orders cascade is not latent: public/app.js:1217 advertises account closure through a support mailto and :882 promises \"We remove your profile and listings\", and with no in-app delete that means a manual operator delete in the Supabase dashboard, which is exactly what fires orders_cattery_id_fkey ON DELETE CASCADE and erases every held, released, and refunded escrow row for that cattery. The first deletion request Cattery receives destroys its own money trail, with no warning to the operator. The fix is three lines in migration 0019, written 2026-07-16 and still untracked and unapplied twelve days on. Real ground was gained against that: 0009 and 0010 were recovered verbatim from the prod migration ledger with provenance headers, and today's canonical audit diffed all 14 prod tables column-for-column against disk and found them identical, closing the standing \"prod may have drifted\" gap. No hard-rule breach: secrets gitignored and untracked, RLS on all 14 tables, screened-badge and buyer-privacy invariants intact.",
